# Borzoi optimization kit — Apptainer / Singularity image made FROM the container image of borzoi/environment/Dockerfile: the same stack and the
# same /kit, for hosts that run Apptainer instead of Docker. The source is the image tagged borzoi-kit:dev in the local Docker daemon (build it
# first: README.md 'Setup', route A); for a published tag the two header lines read `Bootstrap: docker` / `From: <registry>/borzoi-kit:<tag>`.
#   apptainer build borzoi.sif borzoi/environment/apptainer.def
#   apptainer run --nv --cleanenv --bind /path/to/borzoi_data:/data --bind "$PWD/out":/out borzoi.sif \
#     sad --config h100 --mode exact -f /data/hg38.ml.fa -o /out/exact --rc --stats SAD,logSAD -t /opt/borzoi/examples/targets_human.txt -u \
#     /opt/borzoi/examples/params.json /data/f0/model0_best.h5 /kit/borzoi/tests/inputs/example_snvs.vcf
# The image is read-only: give sad an -o on a bound, writable path (the stock script creates it, non-recursively, and refuses an existing one);
# %environment keeps a host user site-packages (PEP 370) from shadowing the pinned stack, --cleanenv keeps the host's variables out.
Bootstrap: docker-daemon
From: borzoi-kit:dev

%post
    mkdir -p /opt/culib && ln -s /.singularity.d/libs/libcuda.so.1 /opt/culib/libcuda.so && ln -s /.singularity.d/libs/libcuda.so.1 /opt/culib/libcuda.so.1

%environment
    export PYTHONNOUSERSITE=1
    # Triton <= 3.5 links its launcher stub with -lcuda: offer the unversioned name when --nv bound only libcuda.so.1
    if [ -z "${TRITON_LIBCUDA_PATH:-}" ] && [ -e /opt/culib/libcuda.so ]; then export TRITON_LIBCUDA_PATH=/opt/culib; fi

%runscript
    cd /kit/borzoi && exec bash /kit/borzoi/run.sh "$@"

%help
    Borzoi optimization kit: drop-in modes that make stock Borzoi variant scoring (borzoi_sad.py of calico/borzoi @ 5c93582 on calico/baskerville
    @ 544073b, TensorFlow 2.15.1) faster without changing how it is called — off = stock exactly; exact (the default, the one kit mode) = identical
    outputs, faster. `apptainer run --nv borzoi.sif <verb> ...` =
    `bash /kit/borzoi/run.sh <verb> ...` (verbs: install, sad, check; /kit/borzoi/README.md inside the image). Requires an NVIDIA driver that
    runs CUDA 12.2 (535 or newer); the genome, targets, params and weights are the command's own arguments on bound paths.
